  body: "# Old industrial schemes and the December 2012 transition\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe old-cases
    chapter describes ending the WC (Supplementation), PB and MDB schemes from 5 December 2012, transferring specified
    existing recipients and pending claims to IIDB.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source retains limited guidance
    on compensation and death benefit and sends new claims for pre-5 July 1948 accidents/diseases to IIDB under
    its rules. This is not proof that every old-scheme paragraph still provides a current claim route.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 73001, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 73002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 73003, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=3).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch73`:
    PDF `3b17129736cf09e79f9df7079d4a83c4c2b74676d356c2c92947ef6cb12839ba`; extracted pages `d3ddd9b78f348565850afeafbaecd17ef9937905318211d171770a38ceadd7a3`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.331056Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8019b540f0b62305b892c3/dmgch73.pdf#page=3
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/industrial-old-compensation
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter explicitly identifies compensation and death-benefit material as retained after the
      transition.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch73/0003
      quote: "73001   WC (Supp) and PB and MDB will not apply from 5.12.121. Therefore, from that date,\n      \
        \  people wishing to claim for\n\n        1.       accidents which happened or\n\n        2.       diseases
        caused by employment\n\n        before 5.7.48 should claim IIDB under the normal rules2. Apart from DMG
        73002 –\n        73003, the only guidance being retained is on other compensation (see DMG 73332\n     \
        \   et seq) and death benefit (see DMG 73412 et seq).\n                                                \
        \                 1 WR Act 12, s 64(2); 2 SS CB Act 92, s 94(1) & 108(1)\n\n\n        People receiving WC
        (Supp) or PB and MDB"
      locator: DMG 73001
  - target: term/iidb-loss-of-faculty
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The transition directs relevant old accident/disease claims to IIDB rather than creating a
      continuing parallel general scheme.
    evidence:
